cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata in this file. The
  associated manuscript is not yet published; once it is, cite the article in
  preference to the software.
title: >-
  Bounded asymmetry profiles for protein disorder distributions: analysis
  pipeline
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a methodological study defining a bounded local
  asymmetry profile S(x) over a continuous feature coordinate, with three scalar
  summaries, evaluated on experimentally curated intrinsic disorder annotations
  for 1,766 proteins from four taxa (DisProt release 2026_06). Regenerates every
  manuscript table, figure and diagnostic from the deposited input files with a
  single command.
type: software
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-07-27"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/innerlightr-wq/disprot-bounded-asymmetry"
url: "https://github.com/innerlightr-wq/disprot-bounded-asymmetry"

identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21628406
    description: >-
      Zenodo archive of the preprint and the original pre-refactor analysis
      files (version v8, published 2026-07-27). Verified to resolve on
      2026-07-27. TODO: replace with the Zenodo concept DOI, which always
      resolves to the latest version; it is available on the record page under
      "Versions -> Cite all versions?".
authors:
  - family-names: "De Jesús"
    given-names: "Elias"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0190-9143"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, Virginia, USA"
    email: "dejesuselias10@gmail.com"
keywords:
  - intrinsically disordered proteins
  - DisProt
  - AlphaFold
  - pLDDT
  - distributional comparison
  - cross-taxon calibration
  - reproducibility

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT YET PUBLISHED
#
# The manuscript in paper/manuscript.pdf has not been accepted by a journal, so
# this file deliberately carries NO journal name, volume, issue, page range or
# article DOI, and no `preferred-citation` block. Every field below is presently
# true. Nothing is a placeholder standing in for a real value.
